clear  situation on the film market  according to deadline the lion king 2  should of course have the highest  priority but on the other hand director  jenkins still has a full schedule and  other projects in the pipeline  especially the post-production will  similar to the first part be a  significant part of the project so we  don't expect a release before mid-2022  the original plan was to bring steven  spielberg's indiana jones 5 to the big  screen last year  however in the end shooting has not even  begun and james mangold has taken over  the director's chair for the long term  after spielberg announced his  resignation in early 2020. many are  still wondering why  after all spielberg has been one of the  most renowned and capable directors in  hollywood for decades in an interview  with den of geek david kepp who also  recently resigned as screenwriter  brought some light into the darkness  especially because the interaction  between spielberg harrison ford  the script and disney turned out to be  extremely difficult in retrospect  nevertheless there was apparently no  scandal behind the scenes  because cap and mangled spoke out on a  professional level whereupon mangled  thought it was the appropriate step to  turn the fifth indiana jones part  completely upside down and start from  scratch  the current start date is still july 28  2022  but fans shouldn't be too sure yet due  to the current situation what do you  think do you give james maygold a chance  or do you think an indiana jones 5  without spielberg is not a real indiana  jones  write us your opinion in the comments  apart from marcus knispel's rather fluff  remake from 2011  conan the barbarian is without a  question one of the classics of the film  world according to deadline  streaming services have been trying to  get the rights for quite some time  first it was amazon's turn but now  netflix has secured the rights the  streaming giant has big plans for the  franchise they are currently looking for  a director and screenwriter for a  potential series but also want to focus  on other projects from the conan  universe in the future an agreement  between netflix and conan properties  international makes this possible it is  now also clear that the amazon series  with game of thrones director miguel  sapochnick which was announced a few  years ago  was of course definitively rejected by  the netflix deal it will be exciting to  see what netflix will turn it into and  we look forward to receiving more  information about the new conan  series the first two seasons of the boys  are now among the most successful amazon  in-house productions as it has now  become known the people in charge have  been working on a spin-off to what is  currently  the hottest superhero series on the  market for quite some time especially  since  genre competitors such as jessica jones  and company have discontinued or put  their projects on ice  the spin-off is supposed to revolve  around the only superhero college in the  usa  and fans can be sure that the series  will once again have a rough and  humorous look similar to the original  craig rosenberg for example who already  wrote the script for the pilot episode  was also signed on as a showrunner he  will be supported by eric kripke  seth rogen evan goldberg and many more  as executive producers while the comic  by garth ennis and derek robertson will  serve as a model not much is known about  the story and the content yet but we  will keep you informed  [Music]  bye

